{#- The age repair of a structured render (FR-CAT-12, FR-PROF-13; #150).

A render introduced characters without an age: one call asks for each one's age, at
temperature 0. The ``system`` block holds the rating guidance (always first, FR-RATE-4), the
custom instructions and the scene; the ``user`` block lists each introduced character with the
clue the render gave. The answer is the call's ``response_schema`` (``{ages: [{name, age}]}``). -#}
{% macro line(entry) -%}
{% if entry.text %}{{ entry.text }}{% else %}{{ entry.name }}:{% if entry.say %} "{{ entry.say }}"{% endif %}{% if entry.do %} *{{ entry.do }}*{% endif %}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% block system %}
{% if rating_guidance %}
## Content rating guidance
{{ rating_guidance }}

{% endif %}
{% if custom_instructions %}
## Custom instructions
{{ custom_instructions }}

{% endif %}
{% if scene %}
## Scene
{{ scene }}

{% endif %}
## Your part
A scene introduced new characters. Give each one a single plausible age in whole years that fits what the scene says about them.
Answer once for each character listed below, with its name copied exactly as listed. A listed group of people gets one entry and one age. Give no entry for anyone else the scene mentions.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{% for intro in introductions %}
- {{ intro.name }}{% if intro.clue %}: {{ intro.clue }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
